# Optional overrides. A new install needs NO .env at all: start the stack, read the setup code from the backend log
# (docker compose logs backend | grep "setup code") and finish the setup wizard in the browser (docs/setup.md).
# The `bootstrap` service generates the database and Redis passwords, APP_ENC_KEY and INTERNAL_SECRET into the
# `bootstrap` volume (back it up: scripts/backup-bootstrap.sh). Settings live in the database and are changed in the
# wizard or under Admin -> Settings. A value set here wins over the database and shows locked there ("From environment"),
# so copy this file to .env only to pin a value, and uncomment only those lines. NEVER commit .env.
# Existing installs: docs/setup.md section 14 before removing anything.
# Secrets may alternatively be provided as Docker secrets via VAR_FILE=/run/secrets/name (compose.secrets.yaml).

# --- Setup wizard steps (set them in the wizard; uncomment only to pin them from here) ---
# Public address of the portal, no path (wizard step 2)
# PUBLIC_URL=https://friend.example.com
# FriendFlix for Plex (docs/plex.md): run with  docker compose -f compose.prod.yaml -f compose.plex.yaml up -d
# (compose.plex.yaml sets MEDIA_SERVER=plex, the plex images and UPDATE_REPO=LetsManu/friendflix-plex), or set
# COMPOSE_FILE=compose.prod.yaml:compose.plex.yaml here and use plain `docker compose up -d`.
# Plex address and token are set in the wizard (media step) or Admin -> Settings; uncomment only to pin them from here.
# Plex base URL as seen from the containers (LAN IP, or http://host.docker.internal:32400 for Plex on this Docker host).
# Backend and gateway both get it from compose.plex.yaml: set for both or for neither, never for one of them.
# PLEX_URL=http://plex.example.com:32400
# Token of the Plex account FriendFlix uses for everybody (a dedicated Plex account is recommended: Plex stores the
# selected audio track per account). Backend only (the gateway gets it from the backend), never sent to browsers.
# Or PLEX_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/plex_token (locks the field in the wizard)
# PLEX_TOKEN=
# JELLYFIN_URL / JELLYFIN_ADMIN_API_KEY are not used with Plex (leave them unset)
# Authentik (wizard step 4; OIDC provider "FriendFlix", redirect URI: ${PUBLIC_URL}/auth/callback)
# OIDC_ISSUER=https://auth.example.com/application/o/friendflix/
# OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Authentik group whose members become portal admins on first login (default friendflix-admins)
# ADMIN_GROUP=friendflix-admins

# --- Per container (compose / env only, not in Admin -> Settings) ---
# NPM reaches the portal on these host ports (bound to BIND_ADDR only, default loopback)
# BIND_ADDR=127.0.0.1
# WEB_PORT=3080
# BACKEND_PORT=3081
# GATEWAY_PORT=3082
# Media server implementation ("plex" in this fork, set by compose.plex.yaml; see docs/architecture.md, "Media server seam")
# MEDIA_SERVER=plex
# Time zone of the backend (digest hour, nightly playback check hour)
# TZ=Europe/Vienna
# Weekly recap: weekday (0 = Sunday ... 6 = Saturday) and server hour (0-23, -1 = off); Admin -> Digest overrides them
# DIGEST_DAY=0
# DIGEST_HOUR=18
# Where prepared downloads / preview clips live: empty = Docker named volume, or an absolute host folder
# (create it first: mkdir -p /mnt/data/friendflix/downloads && chown 1000:1000 /mnt/data/friendflix/downloads)
# DOWNLOADS_PATH=
# PREVIEWS_PATH=
# Background jobs: download preparation + cleanup, audio/subtitle language index, media server session polling. Keep true on the single backend.
# BACKGROUND_JOBS=true
# Admin health page: the gateway's internal address (only /health is called)
# GATEWAY_URL=http://gateway:4000
# Development only: accept an http:// OIDC issuer (an Authentik without TLS). Never in production.
# OIDC_ALLOW_INSECURE=false
# Bearer token for /metrics (docs/monitoring.md)
# METRICS_TOKEN=
# Only for the optional compose.monitoring.yaml (Prometheus + Grafana, docs/monitoring.md); METRICS_TOKEN is required there.
# No default password: Grafana refuses to start without GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD (used on its first start only).
#GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
#GRAFANA_ADMIN_USER=admin
#GRAFANA_PORT=3083
#GRAFANA_ROOT_URL=https://grafana.example.com/
#GRAFANA_COOKIE_SECURE=true
#PROMETHEUS_RETENTION=30d
# Images (compose.prod.yaml): registry owner and tag. FF_TAG picks the release channel:
#   latest  = stable: the newest release (default)
#   nightly = every green commit on main (newer, less proven)
#   1 / 1.1 / 1.1.0 = pin a major line, a minor line or one exact release (a short commit sha pins one build)
# Switching: change FF_TAG, then docker compose -f compose.prod.yaml -f compose.plex.yaml pull && docker compose -f compose.prod.yaml -f compose.plex.yaml up -d.
# Without the opt-in updater FriendFlix never pulls or switches images itself; the channel switch under Admin -> Update
# (setting UPDATE_CHANNEL, stored in the database) only picks what the update check compares with and shows this line.
# FF_REGISTRY=ghcr.io/letsmanu
# FF_TAG=latest
# Opt-in updater (docs/setup.md "Updater"): docker compose -f compose.prod.yaml -f compose.plex.yaml --profile updater up -d
#   Admin -> Update then pulls, cosign-verifies and restarts the FriendFlix services itself (FF_TAG is not needed then);
#   only the docker-proxy service sees the Docker socket. Channel, fixed version (UPDATE_VERSION) and automatic updates
#   (AUTO_UPDATE=off|nightly-window, AUTO_UPDATE_TIME=04:00) are database settings in Admin -> Update.
# UPDATER_URL=http://updater:7070
# every compose file of this stack, comma-separated names in the stack directory (compose.plex.yaml sets compose.prod.yaml,compose.plex.yaml)
# UPDATER_COMPOSE_FILES=compose.prod.yaml,compose.plex.yaml
# Version check repository and image names of the updater (compose.plex.yaml sets the fork's)
# UPDATE_REPO=LetsManu/friendflix-plex

# --- Generated (bootstrap volume). Leave unset on a new install. ---
# Existing installs keep their values here until `docker compose logs bootstrap` shows "from environment" for each
# (removing one earlier generates a new value that does not match the database / the encrypted data).
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# REDIS_PASSWORD=
# APP_ENC_KEY=
# INTERNAL_SECRET=

# --- Settings (Admin -> Settings). Uncomment only to pin a value from here; defaults shown. ---
# Webhooks of the media server and the request service; Admin -> Settings -> General -> Generate new. Unset: webhooks answer 403
# WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Request service (optional; without both, wishes are hidden). Older variable names still work with a deprecation warning.
# REQUESTS_URL=http://requests:5055
# REQUESTS_API_KEY=
# Notifications: shared ntfy channel / Discord webhook; NTFY_BASE_URL = ntfy server for personal topics (default: host of NTFY_URL)
# NTFY_URL=
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=
# NTFY_BASE_URL=
# Web Push (Admin -> Settings -> Push notifications -> Generate key pair, or node scripts/gen-vapid.mjs). Subject: mailto:... or https://..., default PUBLIC_URL
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=
# Optional data sources for the detail page (also Admin -> Data sources)
# TMDB_API_KEY=
# OMDB_API_KEY=
# Chromecast (only with an https PUBLIC_URL and the /media/c/ location from deploy/npm/portal.advanced.conf; false for Plan B). docs/cast.md
# CAST_ENABLED=true
# Post-play screen after a film / the last episode ("You're caught up", suggestions); false = off for everyone. docs/discovery.md
# Also in Admin -> Settings -> Recommendations (applies at once); a value here wins and locks it there.
# POSTPLAY_ENABLED=true
# Offline downloads (docs/downloads.md); false for Plan B (nginx auth_request)
# DOWNLOADS_ENABLED=true
# true: roles without download permission also lose Direct Play (original file stays unreachable; costs transcoding). Height caps always block Direct Play.
# DIRECT_PLAY_REQUIRES_DOWNLOAD=false
# DOWNLOAD_CACHE_MAX_GB=50
# DOWNLOAD_MIN_FREE_GB=2
# DOWNLOAD_PREP_CONCURRENCY=1
# DOWNLOAD_PAUSE_STREAMS=2
# DOWNLOAD_FILE_TTL_HOURS=48
# DOWNLOAD_OFFLINE_GRACE_DAYS=7
# DOWNLOAD_CREATE_PER_HOUR=20
# Recommendation index (docs/discovery.md): how much each feature group counts when item vectors are combined (0-10, 0 = off).
# Expert tuning: RECO_W_* and RECO_COEFFS are set here only (not in Admin -> Settings).
# RECO_W_GENRES=1
# RECO_W_TAGS=0.6
# RECO_W_STUDIOS=0.4
# RECO_W_PEOPLE=0.8
# RECO_W_TEXT=1
# RECO_W_NUMERIC=0.3
# RECO_W_COLLECTION=1.5
# Recommendation engine v2 (docs/discovery.md): v1 = the media server's similar titles (default; with Plex FriendFlix's own genre + cast similarity), shadow = compute v2 next to v1 and only emit comparison metrics, v2 = answer with v2
# RECO_ENGINE, RECO_HALF_LIFE_DAYS and RECO_EXPLORE are also in Admin -> Settings -> Recommendations (applies at once, no restart; the admin
# recommendation card links there). Leave them unset to change them there; a value here wins and locks the field.
# RECO_ENGINE=v1
# Half-life in days of the recency decay of a taste signal (weight * 0.5^(age/half-life))
# RECO_HALF_LIFE_DAYS=120
# Override any scoring coefficient: a JSON object of dotted names, e.g. {"signal.thumbUp2":4,"surface.because.seed":0.6,"rank.lambda":0.8}. Names: docs/discovery.md
# RECO_COEFFS=
# Exploration: share of the slots of a recommendation row that may be filled with a medium-score title (0 = off, the default; 0.1 = about 1 in 10). Logged as aggregate counters by row kind only (docs/discovery.md)
# RECO_EXPLORE=0
# gzip/brotli for JSON API responses >= 1 KB (default true); false if Nginx Proxy Manager already compresses /api
# API_COMPRESSION=true
# Admin health page warning levels
# HEALTH_DISK_WARN_PCT=85
# HEALTH_DISK_CRIT_PCT=95
# HEALTH_DB_WARN_GB=10
# Portal invites also create the Authentik account (enrollment flow + MFA). All three, see docs/authentik.md section 9.
# AUTHENTIK_URL=https://auth.example.com
# AUTHENTIK_API_TOKEN=
# AUTHENTIK_ENROLL_FLOW=friendflix-enrollment
# admin "send password reset": slug of the recovery flow with an e-mail stage
# AUTHENTIK_RECOVERY_FLOW=default-recovery-flow
# slug of the TOTP setup flow
# AUTHENTIK_TOTP_SETUP_FLOW=default-authenticator-totp-setup
# In-app sign-in (no .env needed: Admin -> Settings -> Sign-in). Optional overrides: LOGIN_UI=app|authentik (unset = automatic),
# AUTHENTIK_LOGIN_FLOW=default-authentication-flow, AUTHENTIK_INVALIDATION_FLOW=default-invalidation-flow, PASSKEYS_IN_APP=auto|off,
# LOGIN_COVER_WALL=true|false. See docs/authentik.md section 10a.
# Flows of the account page's Security section (defaults shown): AUTHENTIK_STATIC_SETUP_FLOW=default-authenticator-static-setup,
# AUTHENTIK_WEBAUTHN_SETUP_FLOW=default-authenticator-webauthn-setup, AUTHENTIK_PASSWORD_CHANGE_FLOW=default-password-change,
# AUTHENTIK_EMAIL_CHANGE_FLOW=friendflix-email-change (imported by hand: docs/authentik.md section 10a, step 7).
# LOGIN_UI=app
# LOGIN_COVER_WALL=true
# Sessions: absolute 8 h, expire after 2 h without activity
# SESSION_TTL_SECONDS=28800
# SESSION_IDLE_SECONDS=7200
# Admin -> Update: one-click redeploy via Portainer (see docs/operations.md "Updates aus dem Portal"). Either the webhook ...
# PORTAINER_WEBHOOK_URL=https://portainer.example.com/api/stacks/webhooks/<uuid>
# ... or the API (access token, stack id from the stack's URL):
# PORTAINER_URL=https://portainer.example.com
# PORTAINER_API_KEY=
# PORTAINER_STACK_ID=
# PORTAINER_ENDPOINT_ID=1
# Version check: the token only raises the GitHub rate limit
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Backups (opt-in sidecar: docker compose --profile backup up -d backup; see docs/operations.md "Backups & Wiederherstellung")
# BACKUP_PATH=./backups          # host dir for the dumps, must be writable by uid 70 (chown 70 backups)
# BACKUP_HOUR=3                  # daily run at this hour (container TZ, see TZ)
# BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS=14            # older dumps are deleted (legacy name KEEP_DAYS still works)
# BACKUP_RUN_ON_START=false      # true = also dump once when the container starts
# BACKUP_PGPASSWORD_FILE=        # optional: password file inside the container (default: the bootstrap volume's)
